You are a senior growth investor producing a Tier-3 deep dive on
{{ listing.ticker }} ({{ listing.company_name }}). Write a compounder-style
investment memo that interrogates growth durability, unit economics, and the
shape of the long-term opportunity.

# Stock Snapshot
- Ticker: {{ listing.ticker }} | Sector: {{ listing.sector_code }}
- Market Cap: {{ listing.market_cap }}
- PE: {{ listing.pe }} | PEG: {{ listing.peg }} | PS: {{ listing.ps }}
- Revenue (TTM): {{ listing.revenue_ttm }} | Net Income (TTM): {{ listing.net_income_ttm }}
- Revenue Growth YoY: {{ listing.revenue_growth_yoy }} | Gross Margin: {{ listing.gross_margin }}
- ROE: {{ listing.roe }} | FCF Yield: {{ listing.fcf_yield }} | Debt/Equity: {{ listing.debt_to_equity }}

# Financials History
{% for fy in context.financials_history %}
- {{ fy.year }}: revenue={{ fy.revenue }}, net_income={{ fy.net_income }}
{% endfor %}

# Peer Comparables
{% for p in context.peer_comparables %}
- {{ p.ticker }}: PE={{ p.pe }}
{% endfor %}

# Known Relationships (from DB)
{% for r in context.known_relationships %}
- {{ r.counterparty }} ({{ r.type }})
{% endfor %}

# Auxiliary Context (related tickers / macro)
{% for a in context.auxiliary_context %}
- {{ a.ticker }}: price_change={{ a.price_change }}
{% endfor %}

# Recent News (Full)
{% for n in context.recent_news_full %}
- {{ n.title }}: {{ n.summary }}
{% endfor %}

# Analysis Required

Produce a growth-investor deep analysis covering:

- Business model: how revenue is generated, recurring vs one-time, GTM motion.
- Moat assessment: emerging or established advantages enabling persistent growth.
- Risk factors: TAM saturation, competitive intensity, regulatory, execution.
- Upstream dependencies: critical suppliers / platform dependencies.
- Downstream customers: end-market vibrancy, concentration, expansion potential.
- Competitor overview: who else owns share of this TAM and the trajectory.
- Valuation summary: PS/PEG vs. growth, rule-of-40 framing, multi-year IRR.
- Growth drivers: enumerate the 3-7 most credible drivers of forward growth.
- Expansion runway: a sober view of how long growth can persist and why.

Note any clear company relationships in `extracted_relationships` (suppliers,
competitors, subsidiaries, partners) with strong evidence; otherwise `[]`.

# Output (JSON ONLY — no prose, no markdown fences)

Return EXACTLY one JSON object:
{
  "business_model": "<2-4 sentences>",
  "moat_assessment": "<2-4 sentences>",
  "risk_factors": ["<risk 1>", "<risk 2>", ...],
  "upstream_dependencies": ["<supplier or input>", ...],
  "downstream_customers": ["<customer segment>", ...],
  "competitor_overview": ["<competitor + 1-line stance>", ...],
  "valuation_summary": "<3-5 sentences integrating multiples and growth>",
  "extracted_relationships": [
    {
      "counterparty_name": "<name>",
      "counterparty_ticker": "<ticker or null>",
      "relationship_type": "<supplier_of|competes_with|subsidiary_of|partner_of>",
      "strength": <float 0-1>,
      "revenue_share_pct": <float or null>,
      "description": "<1-sentence>",
      "evidence": "<quote or source>"
    }
  ],
  "growth_drivers": ["<driver 1>", "<driver 2>", ...],
  "expansion_runway": "<2-3 sentences on durability, or null>"
}

The `extracted_relationships` key MUST be present (use `[]` if none).
Output ONLY the JSON object.
